The `SequentialDisposable` class is a thin wrapper around `AtomicReference` and delegates its core operations to static helper methods. Its methods (`update`, `replace`, `dispose`, `isDisposed`) perform minimal work (mostly a single atomic operation), making micro‑benchmarking with JMH unlikely to yield actionable performance insights. Additionally, the class is part of RxJava's internal infrastructure where performance characteristics are already covered by the library's own extensive test suite. Therefore, generating a dedicated JMH benchmark is unnecessary.